%% TAMS -> Video-Understanding -> TADS bridge (see docs/inference-plan.md).
%% Edit this source and re-render:  mmdc -i docs/tads-inference.mmd -o docs/tads-inference.png -b white -s 2
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor VU as Video-Understanding
    participant TAMS
    participant S3 as Storage Backend
    participant TADS
    actor DC as Downstream Consumer

    rect rgb(237, 231, 246)
    Note over VU,TADS: Phase A - setup (schemas are the TADS source of truth)
    Note right of TADS: Provisioning at DEPLOY time (CI / seed job, not VU runtime):<br/>Payload Schemas seeded into TADS with stable external_ids<br/>e.g. vu:transcript:v1, vu:key-moment:v1
    VU->>TADS: GET /schemas?external_id=vu:*:v1 (resolve + cache schema_id per type)
    TADS-->>VU: schema_id per type (startup self-check: fail fast if any missing)
    VU->>TAMS: POST /service/webhooks (subscribe flows/created)
    TAMS-->>VU: webhook flows/created (flow, source_id)
    VU->>TADS: PUT /tracks/{track_id}
    Note over VU,TADS: ONE Track per (Source x analysis-type)<br/>track_id = uuid5(source_id, analysis_type) - deterministic, so PUT is idempotent<br/>schema_id = resolved for that type (a Track validates against exactly one schema)<br/>timeline_reference.entity_id = tams://.../sources/{source_id} (whole Source, no timerange)<br/>allow_overlaps = true (multi-speaker / overlapping detections)
    TADS-->>VU: 201 Created
    VU->>TAMS: POST /service/webhooks (subscribe flows/segments_added, flow_ids filter)
    end

    rect rgb(232, 245, 233)
    Note over VU,TADS: Phase B - per-segment analysis loop (near-live) - transcript + key-moment
    loop For each Flow Segment
        TAMS-->>VU: webhook flows/segments_added (object_id, timerange, get_urls)
        VU->>S3: GET media object (presigned get_url)
        S3-->>VU: media bytes
        Note over VU: analyse (proxy rendition) - ffmpeg demux ONCE into audio + frames<br/>map model seconds to ABSOLUTE timerange = segment_start + relative (from segment timerange)<br/>buffer units that span segment boundaries, anchored to the START segment<br/>event_id = uuid5(track_id, segment_anchor, unit_ordinal) - NOT timerange,<br/>so a timerange refinement upserts instead of orphaning a duplicate
        VU->>TADS: POST /tracks/{track_id}/events (batch array)
        Note over TADS: validate each payload vs its schema (per-event 201 / 400)<br/>upsert on the supplied id (PUT-with-id = replace), so writes are idempotent<br/>reanalysis that changes unit count: DELETE /tracks/{id}/events?ids=... then re-POST
        TADS-->>VU: 200/201 (+ per-event errors)
    end
    end

    rect rgb(255, 243, 224)
    Note over TADS,DC: Phase C - downstream consumer (separate deferred project, shares only vu:*:v1 vocab)
    DC->>TADS: POST /service/webhooks (subscribe tracks/events_added, filter by track/entity/tags)
    loop as events land
        TADS-->>DC: webhook tracks/events_added (event)
        DC->>DC: index for search / surface in UI
        opt data-driven writeback
            DC->>TAMS: POST /flows/{id}/segments (by-reference composition)
        end
    end
    end
